  "records": [
    {
      "id": "i01",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "On the largest scales, cosmology expects the universe to look the same in every direction.",
      "text_sha256": "50b6c1cb04f9e5ae3cf1294f82e9c2f6d8d558b61e60e9326f1499456e28a207",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i01-50b6c1cb04f9.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "316d9b1e72105b753d433f03748359cd90433d740f76ed74f2252d0f92643292",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "4.968000",
          "size": "79488"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i02",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "A conceptual sky of spiral galaxies should therefore show no built-in preference for clockwise or anticlockwise winding.",
      "text_sha256": "db0be38e5a642a8eeaff02dc79f8bdb2a7fede40f1ce785c9c64fc6570e4b738",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i02-db0be38e5a64.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "c6075c6c408a95352da79b2a947096e50ecf98e0676d12b20a3cb8bedcc217bb",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.056000",
          "size": "112896"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i03",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Galaxies acquire angular momentum while surrounding structure grows, so balance is the prediction, not an accident.",
      "text_sha256": "7b63a9b9c192024051536b4c016f1a7c252d2cc5a1b250026b110b01d1964310",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i03-7b63a9b9c192.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "7a2856db533ffd1f3b2c41510430ebc30c1ded35952d450be5a25cdfe013f56c",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.744000",
          "size": "107904"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i04",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "A preference for spiral galaxies in one sector of the sky to be left-handed or right-handed spirals would indicate a parity violating asymmetry in the overall universe and a preferred axis.",
      "text_sha256": "2e44c9feaac73b931ecf5a597aaa00957d750a2ade3a72e6e0d845fb015f0a12",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i04-2e44c9feaac7.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "fa94f8db4e837d8d1c6dacd98fd858e3ec76130875bf61cb674a9d651cc94c04",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "10.272000",
          "size": "164352"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i05l",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Longo reported: An unbinned analysis for a dipole component that made no prior assumptions for the dipole axis gives a dipole asymmetry of \u22120.0408\u00b10.011 with a probability of occurring by chance of 7.9\u00d710\u207b\u2074.",
      "text_sha256": "776d132d23c1d683c93f9ebd98af984b0fdb57e18289302f496bbba689223817",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i05l-776d132d23c1.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "1426d8e48bf177b112f30cedb88078382dbba4c190e53ee1f3452ceccccbf150",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "15.696000",
          "size": "251136"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i05s",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Shamir reported: The results show that the local universe (z<0.3) is not isotropic in terms of galaxy spin, with probability P<5.8\u00d710\u207b\u2076 of such asymmetry to occur by chance.",
      "text_sha256": "c6ba0f9a82ec1286400db81ed56c8511a4194e56d15f00368662ffb775eeeecc",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i05s-c6ba0f9a82ec.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "bfb29ccdff8a881d1a2e100e5c0616dc5c79423b6a520199cf0e2c677cd8375c",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "12.216000",
          "size": "195456"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i05d",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Land and colleagues reported: After establishing and correcting for a certain level of bias in our handedness results we find the winding sense of the galaxies to be consistent with statistical isotropy.",
      "text_sha256": "43f7a971b4e0528027adebc5b4e2fc2ff28bac3b27dd8dd235ec8a7604e1c511",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i05d-43f7a971b4e0.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "0ab844a0efa6729305750ff856891fa9395e38926af5fe3f75de61f3ab40be2c",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "10.704000",
          "size": "171264"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i05u",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "These studies reported incompatible answers, so the literature remains disputed; this video adopts none of them as its finding.",
      "text_sha256": "5d5ed85e1f37befe16c1201085b41f570e360220db9e5dfe31b14c3fb451638b",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i05u-5d5ed85e1f37.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "c46f44d48b428af27c12bcaff5271ea97908bbf781e0e2eba387e184c3661276",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.512000",
          "size": "120192"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i06",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "The catch is that people and algorithms can carry a left-right sorting bias, so the same images need a mirror control.",
      "text_sha256": "b6ba11c74ba5d4bf1b0ad48aa8ae17c2f7210b49e307827a913b83895af4fe5b",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/i06-b6ba11c74ba5.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "610a0607d0e038a117beeda9576dfba9b0558f8f278056d8d443c30a6f769987",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.080000",
          "size": "113280"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "section": "question",
      "text": "Can an apparent imbalance between clockwise and anticlockwise labels be separated from one introduced by the labeling process?",
      "text_sha256": "ee829c9ef24e6e96ca3b73040a8e3ac6b351571b05f9b38d478e4721891c965a",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s02-ee829c9ef24e.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "42fe4e520e2fd0a7ae0de25a7c1bc0dda2f72cd93976f6e63b4bd82ad535f874",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.296000",
          "size": "116736"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "section": "two-worlds",
      "text": "Two explanations can create the same apparent imbalance.",
      "text_sha256": "2654139c78f30dc6ac52754426d248e515600d47aef72f39a0818f5a076abd7f",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s03-2654139c78f3.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "87ef912035fd95327979b57f11fb15a9b0ba867248994bcd8f324dc57405c173",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "3.744000",
          "size": "59904"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "section": "two-worlds",
      "text": "One places the pattern in the images.",
      "text_sha256": "c2f6b0727d046ad77d44d24a9ddd2910ba3fefd3f8dd3b7e4762a1be656bf511",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s04-c2f6b0727d04.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "0735f5db1d7dd967f689a6ec28639239bafc1b3aa8ffea913d961583ffaaaf9d",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "2.856000",
          "size": "45696"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "section": "two-worlds",
      "text": "The other places it in the labeling process.",
      "text_sha256": "798294462935195091a0236873990264bc76d6ada3a22ec1db5760690056f6a2",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s05-798294462935.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "e25fa3d454cb7151d2cd76b20f5cc1c4a8edb39d26cc21b662cce3a1603b0c14",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "2.592000",
          "size": "41472"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "Apply one decisive test to both worlds: mirror the same conceptual spiral horizontally.",
      "text_sha256": "ddb7198d69648c42be73567bf013379d08242dec8f7969258c638002b787455d",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s06-ddb7198d6964.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "c019fccc6882eb9b319ae0915d758f4a56190ce3f42df7bd1461e9017a39076a",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.216000",
          "size": "99456"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "The geometry reverses, and its apparent label inverts from clockwise to anticlockwise.",
      "text_sha256": "4ec7573b3247d00d4b3357c7f77185bcb3383f2e0fe9cfb3049d17e2849ea0c2",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s07-4ec7573b3247.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2f0b36c5d855d740a080394bbf93d51ab6c1faf38d21527157a2891333b9f8c8",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "5.664000",
          "size": "90624"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "If the pattern belongs to the images themselves, it must follow that inversion.",
      "text_sha256": "b7adc8ea224c55c5483515e22ec16c72bfcb8b2bb6e11275866f71b3e58d1be0",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s08-b7adc8ea224c.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "e3b2d9a0ef43898a9bd119e76266b8c1204818e49c1890ab0426baca875cecb1",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "4.008000",
          "size": "64128"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "If it entered through the labeling process instead, it need not follow the pixels.",
      "text_sha256": "0de62cff2934285852f8fcd2fed708bb361076c30f7baac5726582fa26fe0bb3",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s09-0de62cff2934.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "dacb1c93b393068a332219fcb02bc9bb0c9bc08e7217d1880ec3fbe66606897e",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "4.584000",
          "size": "73344"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "One mirror, two incompatible predicted behaviors: that difference is the scientific discriminant.",
      "text_sha256": "3b19d3104719b6e7bdb6b60b6b493507c71e449b6bec1d59d93b8ba4ac9d50fc",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s10-3b19d3104719.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "fa851a12f4e2102d58ec5c7f2bb4acabdd392abdf88208975ede181940f9df65",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1,
            "bit_rate": "128000"
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.008000",
          "size": "112128"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "Before any number was computed, we fixed the mirror logic, every cut, both thresholds, and paired comparisons.",
      "text_sha256": "1d072584576a41abdbe2a591b174a1a08f23bdd5822277e879e304f093bf8cb8",
      "file": "audio_v5/raw/s11-1d072584576a.mp3",
